course: dictionary
lesson: 5609
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the sentence around the word tells you which one is right. The word lift has several. «A cobra lifts the front of its body» means raises it up. «Take the lift to the top floor» means the machine that carries people up and down.
explain: Sometimes a word points to a feeling, not a thing. «Many people feel real relief after confession, like a weight lifted.» Nobody lifted anything heavy here. The weight has gone, so the burden has gone. A lift can also be a happy feeling: «The news gave her a lift.»
explain: Ask: what would fit in this place? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check it still makes sense. A rule can be lifted, which means it is ended. The sentence will tell you which meaning fits, so read the words around the hard one first.
fact: Lift can be a verb (to lift) or a noun (a lift).
fact: To lift means to pick something up and raise it.
fact: A lift is a machine that carries people up and down in a building; Americans call it an elevator.
fact: A lift can also be a free ride in someone's car, or a happy feeling.
fact: To lift a rule or a ban means to end it.
exercise: «A cobra lifts the front of its body and spreads long ribs in its neck.» What does lifts mean here? | A free ride in a car | A happy feeling | Ends a ban | *Picks up and raises
exercise: «Safe lifts, shown by Elisha Otis in the 1850s, stop the lift falling if a cable breaks.» What is a lift in this sentence? | A heavy thing to pick up | *A machine that carries people up and down a building | A free ride in someone's car | A happy feeling
exercise: «The news gave her a lift.» What does a lift mean here? | Ending a rule | Something heavy to pick up | *A happy feeling | A machine in a building
test: «Many people feel real relief after confession, like a weight lifted.» What does lifted mean here? | Raised high in the air | Broken into small pieces | Put inside a machine | *Taken off, so the heavy feeling has gone
test: «Never accept a lift from someone you were not told about.» What is a lift in this sentence? | A happy feeling | Something to pick up and carry | A machine in a building | *A free ride in someone's car
exam: «The council lifted the ban on the park, so people can play there again.» What does lifted mean here? | A ride in a car | A machine for going up and down | *Ended, so the ban no longer applies | Picked up and raised
